//? Title: Deformable Convolution: Learned Sampling and Explicit V1/V2 Fits
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Deformable filters learn where each spatial tap samples, while v2 also learns a modulation mask.
We visualize integer/fractional sampling, verify values and all offset-bias derivatives, then
show separate tensor Adam loops for complete compact v1 and v2 residual networks.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.5_attention_and_modern_convnets/deformable_conv.cpp`.

> The method

For tap k=(ky,kx) and output position p, sampling uses p*stride-pad+dilation*k+(dy,dx).
Offsets are interleaved dy,dx per row-major tap. Four neighboring input pixels contribute
by bilinear weights; pixels outside the image contribute zero. The main filter contracts
sampled tap/channel values into output channels. A zero-initialized biased 3×3 predictor
produces 2K offsets, or 3K outputs for v2 (2K offsets then K logistic masks), with K=k².
Main filters use He-uniform initialization. Prediction uses the main stride and symmetric
padding one; main symmetric pad is dilation*(k−1)/2. A stride-one wrapper keeps image size.

$$y_o(p)=\sum_{k,c}W_{k,c,o}\,m_k(p)\,x_c(p\,s-\mathrm{pad}+d\,k+\Delta_k(p)).$$
\alttext(Each learned filter tap reads a displaced bilinear sample, optionally scales it by a v2 mask, then sums channels and taps.)

A new v1 layer with zero offsets equals ordinary convolution with the same weights.
V2 starts with masks sigmoid(0)=.5, so its BIAS-FREE output is half that convolution.
An optional output bias is added afterward. This amplitude statement is about one layer,
not a complete BN-normalized network. The centre-only diagnostic isolates sampling from
spatial filtering; fractional coordinates check zero-extension rather than border clamping.
An independent host oracle is only a numerical reference: production offset prediction,
sampling, modulation, contraction, losses and fitting use the tensor library.

Bilinear derivatives are piecewise; integer-coordinate boundaries can be nondifferentiable.
The Float64 finite-difference probe uses fractional parts between .2 and .8 so every perturbation
stays on one piece. It checks all eighteen offset-bias coordinates, including sampling near
image boundaries. Native fixtures also check stride one/two and dilation one/two at zero offsets.

The two classifier fits retain all sixteen bottlenecks of quarter-width ResNet-50. A 3×3/1
stem without pooling and first-1×1 stage strides match the compact source. All nine spatial
filters in stages three/four become deformable, operating on 8×8 and 4×4 maps with widths
64/128. The plain 1484186-scalar model gains six*(9*64*maps+maps)+three*(9*128*maps+maps)
predictor scalars, where maps=18 or 27, giving 1608764 for v1 and 1671053 for v2.
Deformable filters are bias-free followed by BN/ReLU; BN epsilon is 1e-5. Other layers use
ordinary symmetric-padded He-uniform convolutions, final global mean and a biased classifier.
The full-model probe checks all learned gradients are finite at the original 32-pixel geometry.

Each visible fit uses 128 fit/64 validation/64 official-test rows, four batch-eight epochs (64 updates, kept short for build time),
Adam(.001), explicit kernel L2=.0001/2 and independent padded crops/flips. Every offset predictor,
mask predictor, main kernel and backbone leaf enters the optimizer. Validation selects paired
learned/BN checkpoints separately for v1 and v2. These small fixed-seed fits do not reproduce
the source's longer training, detection benchmarks or the paper's feature-mimicking objective.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/deformable_conv_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/deformable_conv_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/deformable_conv_concept.tikz > build/deformable_conv_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/deformable_conv_concept.svg build/deformable_conv_concept.dvi > build/deformable_conv_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
